From: Peios Package Maintainers <packages@peios.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] clang: anchor build-tree resources at LLVM_BINARY_DIR

Peios uses /x86_64-linux-peios as LLVM_LIBDIR_SUFFIX.  The resource-header
build rule currently prefixes lib${LLVM_LIBDIR_SUFFIX} with the parent of
LLVM_LIBRARY_OUTPUT_INTDIR.  When the suffix contains a slash, that parent is
already the unsuffixed lib directory and the result gains a second lib path
component:

  build/lib/lib/x86_64-linux-peios/clang/<major>/include

Clang itself correctly derives:

  build/lib/x86_64-linux-peios/clang/<major>/include

Anchor the resource path directly at LLVM_BINARY_DIR, as the runtime resource
rule already does.  This is equivalent for the ordinary empty suffix and also
supports multi-component library suffixes.

---
 clang/lib/Headers/CMakeLists.txt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/clang/lib/Headers/CMakeLists.txt b/clang/lib/Headers/CMakeLists.txt
index 0d88a8da1ea5..d39fa7426f0c 100644
--- a/clang/lib/Headers/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/clang/lib/Headers/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -402,7 +402,7 @@ set(zos_wrapper_files
 )
 
 include(GetClangResourceDir)
-get_clang_resource_dir(output_dir PREFIX ${LLVM_LIBRARY_OUTPUT_INTDIR}/.. SUBDIR include)
+get_clang_resource_dir(output_dir PREFIX ${LLVM_BINARY_DIR} SUBDIR include)
 set(out_files)
 set(generated_files)
 
-- 
